    summary: 'Students read an abridged adaptation of Shakespeare\'s The Tragedy of Julius Caesar, focusing on themes of friendship, betrayal and leadership; how a historical drama shapes our view of history; and the difference between reading and viewing a play. They write a persuasive essay judging Caesar as a leader and study active and passive voice, frequently confused words, and Greek and Latin roots and suffixes.',
